  "_coverage": "1400 ticks, match still Playing at the end so nothing stops being exercised. Player 0 defends lane 0 with four splash and one single-target beside column 6, which is where the route actually runs (probed, not guessed -- an earlier draft put towers where nothing walked and recorded a match with zero kills). Player 1 mass-sends into it: 20 swarm on tick 400, 12 more on 700, 3 runners on 900, and a full 22-creep burst on tick 1390 that is still on the board at the final tick, which is what lets the replay assert a wave is N distinct creeps rather than one creep wearing N health bars. Player 0 ends on 16 lives / 34 kills, so splash genuinely engaged the waves rather than the separation being tested against an empty lane. MEASURED SENSITIVITY: changing SPAWN_SETBACK from 0.45 to 0.31 moves this hash and does NOT move match-01's. match-01 ends with no live creeps, so sub-tile spawn offsets wash out of it entirely -- this fixture is the only one that pins them.",
